{"latest_judgment":{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_47_570157602#9_1214274043","relevance":3,"reason":"The document is about shopping addiction and directly explains that people may spend money because shopping produces euphoria that covers sadness or anger, or as a way to cope with stress. This is direct evidence that mood and emotional states affect buying/spending behavior.","learned":"Shopping can be used to regulate mood: some people spend to cover sadness or anger, cope with stress, or seek excitement/euphoria."},"action":{"op":"next","qid":"q2965","reason":"The mood-shopping-spending query is producing direct evidence on emotional states affecting shopping and spending, so additional ranked results may yield more grade-3 documents."}}
{"request":{"op":"next","qid":"q2965"},"response":{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_54_1649329265#11_3628563228","ok":true,"op":"next","qid":"q2965","rank":3,"snippet":"for Shopping Addiction Cognitive Behavioral Therapy Managing Shopping Addiction Shopping Addiction Support Groups Shopping Addiction Hotlines Treating Shopping Addiction and Co-Occurring Disorders Compulsive Spending Recovery and Outlook \" , \"segment\": \"Not everyone with a mental health condition that responds to medication requires medication to treat it. However, psychiatric medications can be an important part of treatment for anxiety, depression and other mental health conditions. They may also alleviate symptoms of shopping addiction. Research shows that citalopram and other antidepressant medications can reduce urges to shop in people with a <cover>shopping addiction — especially people with comorbid mood and anxiety disorders. Compulsive Spending </cover>Recovery and Outlook Recovery from compulsive spending is possible. While research has not yet established a clear prognosis or recovery rate for shopping addiction, it does show that many people completely overcome the disorder. As with any other addiction, participating in treatment and building a strong support system are essential elements of recovery. In time, and with persistence, people can replace shopping with other activities that are even more joyful and address the underlying causes of their addiction. If you or a loved one struggle with a substance use disorder and a co-occurring "}}
{"request":{"judgments":"25/50"}}
{"latest_judgment":{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_54_1649329265#11_3628563228","relevance":2,"reason":"The document is about shopping addiction and mentions that urges to shop can be reduced by antidepressants, especially among people with comorbid mood and anxiety disorders. This relates mood/mental state to shopping urges, but the passage is mainly about treatment and does not directly explain how ordinary mood affects buying behavior.","learned":"Shopping addiction may be associated with mood and anxiety disorders, and treating those conditions can reduce urges to shop."},"action":{"op":"next","qid":"q2965","reason":"The current query has already produced multiple direct results about mood, shopping, and spending, so continuing is likely to uncover more grade-3 evidence."}}
{"request":{"op":"next","qid":"q2965"},"response":{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_39_1021036579#16_2047906352","ok":true,"op":"next","qid":"q2965","rank":4,"snippet":"actually mean? And when to use them? iPhone Emoji Meanings: What emojis actually mean? And when to use them? ? Slightly Smiling Face Emoji ? Upside-down Smiling Emoji Smiling Face Emoji ? Smiling Emoji with Eyes Opened ? Smiling Emoji with Smiling Eyes ? Smiling Face with Tightly Closed Eyes ? Smiling with Sweat Emoji ? Tears of Joy Emoji ? Smirk Face Emoji ? Unamused Face Emoji ? Sad Face Emoji ? Relieved Emoji ? Money Face Emoji \" , \"segment\": \"Money Face Emoji The money face emoji sends out a strong message. It signifies spending power. Use this emoji when you’re in the <cover>mood to do some shopping or spending. </cover>It could be an adventure, a pleasure trip, or something that requires spending money. This emoji will attract some attention so be ready whenever you use it. Jessica Hi there! I'm Jessica. My interests include data analysis, IoT, and of course the latest smart devices.\" , \"start_char\": 5401.000000 , \"title\": \"iPhone Emoji Meanings: What emojis actually mean? And when to use them? - ESR Blog\" , \"url\": \"https://www.esrgear.com/blog/iphone-emoji-meanings/\" }"}}
