{"latest_judgment":{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_44_570818059#2_1349215497","relevance":2,"reason":"The document is dedicated to compulsive shopping and directly notes that people with mood and anxiety disorders often exhibit compulsive shopping symptoms, but it does not clearly explain ordinary mood states affecting buying decisions or spending behavior.","learned":"Compulsive shopping can be associated with mood disorders, anxiety disorders, and low impulse control, but this passage is more diagnostic than explanatory."},"action":{"op":"next","qid":"q2974","reason":"The impulse-shopping mood query has already surfaced relevant spending-behavior documents and may retrieve more direct evidence that mood changes impulse buying or shopping behavior."}}
{"request":{"op":"next","qid":"q2974"},"response":{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_44_570818059#3_1349217219","ok":true,"op":"next","qid":"q2974","rank":4,"snippet":"3_1349217219\" , \"end_char\": 3140.000000 , \"headings\": \"Compulsive Shopping Compulsive Shopping What Is Compulsive Shopping? Understanding Compulsive Shopping Key Takeaways Diagnosing Compulsive Shopping Example of Compulsive Shopping Treatment for Compulsive Shopping \" , \"segment\": \"It can also be a symptom of serious mental ailments, such as bipolar disorder. Therapy and antidepressant medication can help in the treatment of compulsive shopping. Diagnosing Compulsive Shopping Compulsive shoppers typically are insecure people with low self-esteem and low <cover>impulse control. Not surprisingly, people with mood, anxiety, and eating disorders often exhibit symptoms. Sometimes compulsive shopping </cover>can also manifest itself as part of a much more severe illness, such as obsessive-compulsive disorder. 1 ﻿ Much as bulimics will purge meals after overeating, compulsive shoppers are known to throw away their purchases. Some research shows a link between attention deficit disorders and compulsive shopping. 3 ﻿ Circumstantial factors have also been found to cause compulsive shopping behavior. Examples of such circumstances include avoidance coping, negation, and isolating factors. 4 ﻿ Compulsive shopping is not the same as retail therapy, the occasional shopping binge in which many people indulge.\" , \""}}
{"request":{"judgments":"39/50"}}
{"latest_judgment":{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_44_570818059#3_1349217219","relevance":2,"reason":"The document is dedicated to compulsive shopping and notes that people with mood, anxiety, and eating disorders often exhibit symptoms, and distinguishes compulsive shopping from retail therapy. It is related evidence, but the visible passage is more about diagnosis than directly answering how mood affects buying things.","learned":"Compulsive shopping is associated with mood and anxiety disorders, but this source does not clearly explain everyday mood effects on purchase decisions."},"action":{"op":"query","query":"(^ emotions influence purchase decisions)","reason":"Search for a direct consumer-psychology formulation likely to retrieve documents explicitly explaining that emotions or mood influence purchase decisions."}}
{"request":{"op":"query","query":"(^ emotions influence purchase decisions)"},"response":{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_31_872412108#10_1758052581","ok":true,"op":"query","qid":"q2975","rank":1,"snippet":"B2B Marketing Case Study Marketing Best Practices for B2B Brands 22. Postcards Pros of Postcard Marketing for B2B Cons of Postcard Marketing for B2B Postcard Marketing Best Practices for B2B Marketing 23. Direct Mail Marketing Pros of Direct Mail for B2B Marketing Cons of Direct Mail for B2B Marketing Direct Mail Marketing Best Practices for B2B Brands Customer Experience (CX): The Golden Thread That Ties B2B Marketing Strategies Together B2B Marketing Strategies: Choose Yours Wisely \" , \"segment\": \"This means purchase decisions are mainly based on facts and logic. In B2C circles, <cover>emotions drive personas and influence purchase decisions </cover>so the deal happens fast. 3. Strategies Generally, because B2B buyers usually decide based on facts and logic, marketers build tactics around educating their target audience. While B2C marketing also involves educating, it’s not always necessary. In this vertical, edutainment that tugs at the emotions works better. 4. Purchase Process Fourthly, B2B buyers have to confer with decision-makers before making a purchase and usually prefer working with an account manager during and after purchase. By comparison, B2C buyers rarely have to discuss their purchase decision with anyone and prefer to purchase directly. 5.\" ,"}}
